  "[curious] Eleven thousand a month between them. Two hundred and forty dollars in checking on the twenty-third. And Mark still says they're fine.",
  "He's right about one thing. Every bill gets paid. Mortgage, daycare, the car: seventy-four hundred, on time, every month.",
  "But Nina's right too. The thirty-six hundred left after the bills just goes, and nothing gets saved.",
  "[thoughtful] Most couples think the fix is earning more. It isn't. It's the order.",
  "On payday, a thousand goes to savings first.",
  "The other twenty-six hundred becomes one number for each day: about eighty-five dollars.",
  "Seventy dollars over on Thursday? The rest of the week drops to about sixty a day, and it still works.",
  "[warm] Now, on the twenty-third, there's a thousand saved, and about seven hundred left for the last week. So Mark was right. They're fine. For real this time.",
  "Save first. Then spend what's safe. Try it at Divvyup dot com."
